From 9985ea338e1cbd05be929737bd712fde70a3daa3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:48:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 848/850] perf(startup): prune unreachable TileLang kernel
 declarations

Propagate non-module _router_indices_dtype / _router_max_rows from the MoE
router to routed_experts in fused_moe/layer.py so TileLangMoE declares
moe_dispatch_v41 only for the router's actual index dtype (int64 on V4.1,
dropping 20 dead int32 dispatch kernels: 353 -> 333 model calls).

Apply the runner's RUNNER_IDX_DTYPE (int64) and aligned-stride _runs_for_strides
selection (matching tilelang_sampling.py) across tilelang_logprob, tilelang_bias,
tilelang_controls, tilelang_auxiliary, tilelang_thinking, tilelang_topk_ids,
tilelang_rejection, rejection_sampler_utils, and tilelang_inputs, dropping 121
unreachable step-kernel specializations (301 -> 180 step calls; total 654 -> 513,
-21.6%) while preserving lazy JIT fallback for non-runner test inputs.

Update the four warmup-declaration unit tests to assert the stride-aware runner
contract.
